        {
          "id": 668629541,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There are quite a few checks already run if you install the git commit_hook, then obviously the pipelines do lots of checks.  'Code Checks + Clang Warnings' does run check_typed_item_calls.py (without --consecutive), but will only error and fail the pipeline for obvious/clear bugs.\n\nI have written a few scripts (tools/check_*.py) that I re-run periodically.  But we don't want to make it too cumbersome for someone to contribute code, or for people to worry about lots of warnings that may be harmless.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
